    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting to individual pace and style, offering step-by-step explanations for tough topics. They can generate practice problems tailored to a student’s level and provide instant feedback. This makes math more engaging and accessible, especially for those who struggle with traditional methods."
